+	 * "SSR before shutdown: scheduling teardown work" as the last line ever,
+	 * with no coredump created, i.e. rproc_stop() never returned.  T1 vs T0
+	 * (in the notifier) discriminates "the work ran and blocked" from
+	 * "the work never got a worker".  Every line contains "SSR " so the
+	 * soak's /dev/kmsg filter picks it up, and dev_err so console-ramoops
+	 * has it too.
